## 1. From Scratch to C

In Week 0 you used **Scratch** (visual blocks). Week 1 moves to **C** — a text-based, compiled language.  
The same core ideas still apply: variables, loops, conditions, functions — just different syntax.

| Scratch | C Equivalent |
|---|---|
| `say "Hello"` | `printf("Hello\n");` |
| `set x to 0` | `int x = 0;` |
| `repeat 10` | `for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)` |
| `if <condition>` | `if (condition)` |

> **Why learn C?** It teaches how memory and hardware actually work. Most modern languages (Python, Java) are built on top of C concepts.

