## 2. Hello, World!

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

### Line-by-Line Breakdown

| Line | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `#include <stdio.h>` | Import the Standard I/O library (gives you `printf`) |
| `int main(void)` | Entry point — every C program starts here |
| `{ }` | Curly braces define the body/block of code |
| `printf("Hello, World!\n");` | Print to screen. `\n` = newline. `;` ends every statement |
| `return 0;` | Signal to the OS that the program finished successfully |

