## 7. Operators

### Arithmetic

```c
int a = 10, b = 3;

a + b   // 13  — addition
a - b   // 7   — subtraction
a * b   // 30  — multiplication
a / b   // 3   — integer division (truncates decimals!)
a % b   // 1   — modulo (remainder)
```

> ⚠️ `10 / 3 = 3` in C, **not** `3.33`. Cast to float: `(float)10 / 3 = 3.33`

### Shorthand Assignment

```c
x += 5;   // x = x + 5
x -= 2;   // x = x - 2
x *= 3;   // x = x * 3
x /= 2;   // x = x / 2
x++;      // x = x + 1
x--;      // x = x - 1
```

### Comparison (return `true` / `false`)

```c
x == y   // equal to
x != y   // not equal to
x >  y   // greater than
x <  y   // less than
x >= y   // greater than or equal
x <= y   // less than or equal
```

### Logical

```c
x && y   // AND — both must be true
x || y   // OR  — at least one must be true
!x       // NOT — inverts true/false
```

