## 8. Conditionals

### if / else if / else

```c
int score = 85;

if (score >= 90)
{
    printf("Grade: A\n");
}
else if (score >= 80)
{
    printf("Grade: B\n");
}
else
{
    printf("Grade: C or below\n");
}
```

### switch

Use `switch` when checking one variable against many constant values.

```c
char grade = 'B';

switch (grade)
{
    case 'A':
        printf("Excellent!\n");
        break;
    case 'B':
        printf("Good job!\n");
        break;
    default:
        printf("Keep trying!\n");
}
```

> ⚠️ Always include `break;` — without it, execution **falls through** to the next case.

### Ternary Operator

```c
// condition ? value_if_true : value_if_false
string result = (score >= 60) ? "Pass" : "Fail";
```

