## 9. Loops

### while — use when count is not known in advance

```c
int i = 0;
while (i < 5)
{
    printf("i = %i\n", i);
    i++;
}
```

### do-while — body always runs at least once (great for input validation)

```c
int n;
do
{
    n = get_int("Enter a positive number: ");
}
while (n <= 0);
```

### for — use when you know the exact count

```c
// for (init; condition; update)
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++)
{
    printf("Row %i\n", i);
}
```

### Loop Comparison

| Loop | Best When | Runs At Least Once? |
|---|---|---|
| `while` | Count unknown | No |
| `do-while` | Must run once (input validation) | **Yes** |
| `for` | Exact count known | No |

### Nested Loops — Mario Pyramid Example

```c
int height = 4;

for (int i = 1; i <= height; i++)
{
    // print spaces
    for (int j = 0; j < height - i; j++)
        printf(" ");

    // print hashes
    for (int k = 0; k < i; k++)
        printf("#");

    printf("\n");
}
```

**Output:**
```
   #
  ##
 ###
####
```

