## 12. Memory, Overflow & Type Casting

### Integer Overflow

Every type has a max value. Exceeding it **wraps around** unexpectedly.

```c
int x = 2147483647;   // max int
x = x + 1;
// x is now -2147483648  ← overflow!
```

### Floating-Point Imprecision

Computers can't represent all decimals exactly in binary.

```c
printf("%.20f\n", 0.1 + 0.2);
// 0.30000000000000004441  (not exactly 0.3)
```

### Type Casting

Force one type to behave as another.

```c
int a = 1, b = 3;

// Without cast — integer division
printf("%i\n", a / b);         // 0

// With cast — decimal division
printf("%.2f\n", (float) a / b);  // 0.33
```

