### Key Rules to Remember

| Rule | Example |
|---|---|
| Every statement ends with `;` | `int x = 5;` |
| Strings use `" "`, chars use `' '` | `"hello"` vs `'h'` |
| `=` assigns, `==` compares | `x = 5;` vs `x == 5` |
| `int / int` truncates | `10 / 3 = 3` |
| Cast to get decimals | `(float)10 / 3 = 3.33` |
| Always `#include` before using library functions | `#include <stdio.h>` |
| Prototypes go before `main()` | `int square(int n);` |

